WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:03.569
-Today was World Water Day,

00:00:03.569 --> 00:00:06.206
so shout-out to my hose!

00:00:07.674 --> 00:00:09.842
Scollins.

00:00:09.842 --> 00:00:12.679
Ruins World Water Day.

00:00:12.679 --> 00:00:14.381
And, you know,
he thinks he's very clever,

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:18.384
but, uh, I saw
how you spelled the joke.

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:20.720
Today was
National Agriculture Day,

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:23.889
so shout-out to my hoes!

00:00:23.889 --> 00:00:26.359
Scollins again.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:28.127
Back-to-back days.

00:00:28.127 --> 00:00:29.863
Turns in the same joke.

00:00:31.531 --> 00:00:34.167
And finally, today was
National Cheesesteak Day.

00:00:34.167 --> 00:00:36.770
Celebrate by taking a Whiz.

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:41.808
Three days in a row
from Scollins.

00:00:41.808 --> 00:00:43.009
A Turkey.

00:00:46.245 --> 00:00:47.514
We gotta say -- I mean, again,

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:49.949
I think if you're
one of our loyal viewers,

00:00:49.949 --> 00:00:52.885
Mike Scollins, for three days in
a row, has written a joke

00:00:52.885 --> 00:00:55.054
about whatever
national day it was.

00:00:55.054 --> 00:00:56.622
And now, you have to
tune in tomorrow

00:00:56.622 --> 00:00:58.591
to see if he can get
four in a row.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:01:01.027
The rare Hambone,
I believe it's called.

00:01:02.495 --> 00:01:04.130
So, hopefully for Scollins,

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:07.200
tomorrow is
National Hacky Joke Day.

00:01:09.468 --> 00:01:10.870
And finally, today was --

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:12.639
Ooh, actually,
before I tell this joke --

00:01:12.639 --> 00:01:16.208
There's a lot of national days
on the calendar.

00:01:16.208 --> 00:01:19.445
Pretty much every day
in the set-ups of our jokes,

00:01:19.445 --> 00:01:21.281
you find out
what national day it is.

00:01:21.281 --> 00:01:23.683
And something that's never
been attempted before

00:01:23.683 --> 00:01:24.917
has happened this week.

00:01:24.917 --> 00:01:27.520
Mike Scollins, a writer
for the show, has told

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:29.922
a "today was national
whatever day"

00:01:29.922 --> 00:01:32.225
with a punch line
three days in a row,

00:01:32.225 --> 00:01:34.927
which is known as a Turkey.

00:01:34.927 --> 00:01:36.695
No one's ever done
four in a row,

00:01:36.695 --> 00:01:38.731
but he's about to try,

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:42.435
and we're about to see if he can
tell four funny jokes

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.103
about a national day
of the week.

00:01:44.103 --> 00:01:45.370
For those who don't know,
this is our friend

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:46.405
Mike Scollins right here.

00:01:46.405 --> 00:01:48.074
Let's just show him off.
There you go.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.510
[ Laughter ]

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.579
That's Mike
in his every-day outfit.

00:01:54.046 --> 00:01:55.815
And now,
we're gonna find out...

00:01:55.815 --> 00:01:58.318
if he can
"tank-top" himself.

00:02:00.886 --> 00:02:02.422
[ Laughs ]

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.858
And finally,
today was Pecan Day.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:07.193
Well, I hope you got a nut.

00:02:08.961 --> 00:02:09.962
Judges?

00:02:09.962 --> 00:02:11.898
[ Pins clattering ]

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.736
Ahh.

00:02:19.071 --> 00:02:20.373
Heartbreaking.

00:02:21.740 --> 00:02:22.742
[ Laughs ]

